  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Storage facilities for raw materials Mozambique</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With a loan from DGGF, Wester Participaties B.V. - Cornelderenabled it to expand its activities in Mozambique. To this end, it has to invest in storage capacity and has entered into a partnership with a South African partner. 2 storage facilities are being set up in Beira and machipanda. Both locations will contain both open storage and closed warehouse storage. With these locations, the hinterland of Mozambique and surrounding countries (Zimbabwe, Zambia, Malawi, etc.) can be accessed. The plans deliver a direct impact in employment through 100-200 jobs and provide indirect job growth of an expected 300. The investments also ensure a further professionalization of the infrastructure.This project clearly contributes to the reconstruction of infrastructure in the port of Beira, which was severely damaged by Hurricane Idai in March 2019.</narrative>
  </description>
